    "questionText": "Prove by mathematical induction that for all positive integers $n$, $1 + 3 + 5 + \\cdots + (2n-1) = n^2$.",
    "solution": "Base case $n=1$: LHS $= 1$, RHS $= 1^2 = 1$. Assume true for $n=k$: $1+3+\\cdots+(2k-1)=k^2$. For $n=k+1$: add $(2(k+1)-1)=2k+1$ to both sides: $k^2 + 2k + 1 = (k+1)^2$. Hence true for all $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+$.",
